    fix(test): existing-tag refusal test uses a test-local tag (hermetic in CI)
    
    The v1.2.0 probe failed in CI two ways: checkouts don't fetch tags, and the
    script's gh call crashes without a token before the refusal branch. The tag
    check runs before any network access, so create/remove a local v9.9.9-test
    tag instead — identical assertion, no CI dependency.
    
    ch:trace row=RELEASE-TJ-008 spec=docs/releasing.md test=tests/test_release_workflow.py::test_check_script_fails_clearly_on_existing_tag evidence=commit witness=live:CI-follow-up
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
